  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything, because removing `channel` from `OrderPlaced` would break ARCH-4.\n\n`OrderPlaced` is consumed by billing-service and analytics-ingest, which live in other repos. I can only see that nothing in this repo reads `channel`. I can't tell whether either consumer does, and ARCH-4 says changes to these events must be additive, with removals going through deprecation. Dropping the field outright could break a deployed consumer.\n\nThe order model has a related problem. `channel` is part of the `POST /orders` request (`src/api/requestParsing.ts`) and is validated in `src/core/order.ts`. Removing it from the model means deciding what happens to clients that still send it. I'd also need to check whether `GET /orders/{id}` returns it, since web-storefront depends on that response (ARCH-8).\n\nHere are the options:\n1. **Deprecate first (my recommendation).**\n   - Mark `channel` as deprecated in `src/core/events.ts` and keep emitting it.\n   - Make it optional in the model and stop validating it on input.\n   - Remove it from the event later, once billing-service and analytics-ingest confirm they don't use it.\n2. **Remove it everywhere now.** Do this only if you confirm both consumers have stopped reading `channel` and that web-storefront doesn't use it. I'd then remove it from the event, model, parsing, validation, tests and docs.\n3. **Remove it from the model only.** I'd keep the event field and populate it with a fixed placeholder value. That is hacky and I wouldn't do it without your say-so.\n\nWhich option do you want? If it's option 2, tell me the consumers have confirmed.",
